{"id": "WR18-2", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**No documented way to declare a database index.** Searched \"index filter column\", \"identifier unique\"; the agent-docs only list indexes among RDBMS model contents. Found by diffing: `DataMember.identifier=true` makes the generator create a (non-unique) btree index (`IDX_<hash>` on `c_sku`). Foreign-key columns (`c_category_id`, `c_seller_id`, `c_product_id` of order lines) get no index. F80 stayed under 1 s without a model index (warm); a cold first call after a start took 1.2 s. The \"indexes on filter columns\" part of F80 is therefore not done through the model (see \"not done\"). "}
{"id": "WR18-3", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**`filterBy(String)` cannot navigate relations** (documented as \"NOT supported\") and there is no inverse relation from `CustomerAccount` to its orders / reviews / quotes. For \"all rows of this customer\" the doc gives no pattern. Used: a derived attribute `customerEmail` on the entity (`Review`, `PointsEntry`, `GiftCard.buyerEmail`; `SalesOrder` and `Quote` had one) and the typed `filterByCustomerEmail`. Costs a model change per entity; the practice's remark \"every relation that points at the person must be listed in the delete service\" has no helper to find them (looked up in PostgreSQL `pg_constraint` instead). "}
{"id": "WR18-4", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**Aggregations (counts per group) are not possible with the DAO; the doc's answer is native SQL** (\"No platform precedent: isolate in one service\"). It works (`@Reference DataSource` found exactly one service in Karaf; the test kit binds one too, HSQLDB runs the same SQL). Missing in the doc: that unquoted `t_webshop_*` / `c_*` names work on both PostgreSQL and HSQLDB, that enumerations are stored from 1 (`ordinal()+1`), that `avg()` of an integer column truncates on HSQLDB (cast to double precision). "}
{"id": "WR18-5", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**A transient relation from an unmapped output TO to a mapped TO works** (`SearchResult.items -> ShopProductInfo`, filled with `ShopProductInfoDao.findAllById(ids, mask)`), and the response carries `__signedIdentifier` for each item. Not in the docs (custom-operations.md only shows flat outputs); found by trying. "}
{"id": "WR18-6", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**`judo validate --strict` passes but the Maven UI validation fails** when `fill` puts an INSTANCE operation with a file output (`exportMyData`) and one with an input (`eraseAccount`) into the view of a derived singleton access: \"ActionContainerSameWithActionDefinition / NamedElementHaveToBeInApplication\". The build only prints \"Verify UI model is presented has failed\" (detail only with `-DvalidateModels=true` on the module). Fix used: delete the two operation forms from the view (the custom panel calls the operations through the generated service). The CLI validate should run the same UI validation. "}
{"id": "WR18-7", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**Build cache hides the cause**: with `-DuseCache=true` (quick mode default of `judo.sh build`) the frontend-react model step fails with only `{}: {}` and \"Verify UI model is presented\"; `-DuseCache=false -DvalidateModels=true` shows the real error (R18-6). "}
{"id": "WR18-8", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**`create -t MenuItemAccess` is refused (\"created automatically\")** but the auto-created item gets the TO name as label (\"PrivacyInfo\", \"ProductVersionInfo\"); rename with `update webshop::<Actor>::Menu_<n> -s label=...`. R17's script line `create -t MenuItemAccess` also did nothing then (the item came with the access). `query esm` / `fq` list at most 800 hits: later members are silently missing (this hid `PrivacyInfo` members, `keep` left them in). "}
{"id": "WR18-9", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**Zeta engine / YAML**: `agent-docs/model/model-validation-and-transformation.md` says ZETA is the default and `-Djudo.transformation.mode=ZETA|ETL|DUAL` selects; nothing about a YAML option for the build. The build log shows \"using Zeta engine\" for all steps (only \"Zeta ASM to Script\" falls back to ETL, \"not yet implemented\"). Used the default. "}
{"id": "WR18-10", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**Interceptors in the app module**: the catalog puts interceptors in the generated `interceptors` module. An interceptor that must share a service with custom operations (`ProductVersions`) can live in the app module with `judo-runtime-core-dispatcher` as a `provided` dependency (fragment `app/pom.xml.extra-dependencies.fragment.hbs`); worked. The test kit offers `fixture.addInterceptor(...)`, not used (DAO calls in tests do not trigger interceptors anyway). "}
{"id": "WR18-11", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**Home page with server-side paging breaks old specs' assumption \"all products are on the home\"**: specs find a product card on the home; with 24 per page they only work because the default sort is newest first (test products are created just before). The \"Seller\" facet of a volume catalogue is a top-12 list (counts need SQL per value); the category chips are not limited (40). "}
{"id": "WR18-12", "src": "webshop-R18", "target": "", "text": "**Schema upgrade is not part of `judo.sh start`**: after a model change `schema_dir=application ./judo.sh schema-upgrade` must be run before `start` (as in R17); the build alone leaves the old schema (the new table was missing). The doc says so, but `build` printing success makes it easy to forget. ### Round 18: not done / open (written at the R18 deadline) - **Two smoke tests failed after R18 (F71, F76 + F77): cause found in round 19 (R19-6)**: the checkout took about 20 s because the derived members of `CustomerAccount` join over tables without foreign-key indexes and the dev database has ~1 800 accounts (the specs wait 20 s for the order). F71 passed alone once (a faster moment), F76 failed alone, and passed with the hand-made indexes of `scripts/dev-indexes.sql`. Not a defect of the R18 code, but a data-volume problem that the model cannot fix (R18-2). - **Flaky (passed alone after failing in the serial run)**: `overhaul UI15 checkout as steps` (failed at `getByTestId('cart')` after an add from the product page, passed alone in 1.1 min). Cause: not found; shared data of 3 earlier runs (many carts / orders of earlier tests), timing of the cart page. - **Old specs adapted to the paged home (R18-11)**: `showProduct` (header search) in `helpers-customer.ts` for `addFromCard` / `addFromDetails`, `catalog-home` S08 (Footwear category, sort by name), `overhaul` (showProduct), `typeInto` uses `.first()` because the admin product page has a read-only \"Price label\" field that also matches `/^Price/`. - **F80 \"indexes on filter columns\"**: not done through the model (R18-2); measured < 1 s warm without one. - **F81**: sellers facet shows the 12 largest sellers only; price buckets are fixed (0-25, 25-50, 50-100, 100-250, 250+); rating facet is \"average >= n\". - **F82**: the query counts all orders of all customers (not only the visible ones); only sub-order shipments are not involved. Product page shows the section only when there is something to show. - **F83**: versions are created on update through the admin / seller screens, on bulk price change and when an order is placed; products changed by the import (F79) get their first version at the first order or the first edit. No restore-old-version function. - **F84**: the Keycloak user of the erased customer is NOT deleted (no admin client in the app); a later login with the same user creates a fresh account. Sellers are refused (SELLER_ACCOUNT). Orders of companies keep the company link. - **F85**: the file conta"}
{"id": "WR19-1", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**\"Verify UI model is presented\" again for the operation forms of a derived singleton access** (R18-6): `ReportInfo` (ops `run`, `pdf`) needed the same deletion of the generated operation forms from the view. `judo validate --strict` says passed, only the Maven UI validation fails. Still no way to tell `fill` not to place them. "}
{"id": "WR19-2", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**Hand-written data changeset: the doc's table / column names are wrong for this project and the flow needs two goals.** `schema-evolution.md` / `migration-backfill-default-where-null.md` say `T_ENTITIES_<NAME>` / `C_<NAME>`; this project's tables are `t_webshop_<entity>` with `c_<attribute>` (checked with `\\\\d`). `judo.sh schema-upgrade` generates and applies in one step (the doc says so); the way to insert a changeset is the plugin goals `judo-rdbms-schema:generate` then `:execute` (`mvnd judo-rdbms-schema:generate -DjdbcUrl=... -DupdateModel=...webshop-rdbms_postgresql.model -f application/schema`), which `judo.sh` does not expose and the doc does not name (found with `-Dgoal` listing: `apply, execute, generate`). Worked: four old addresses split, data kept. "}
{"id": "WR19-3", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**Compose: no way found to create the schema of an EMPTY PostgreSQL database.** `judo-rdbms-schema:apply` needs the `JUDO_MODEL_VERSIONS` table; the application does not create the schema on start (the app answered 200 with no tables). The dev flow gets its first schema inside the Maven build. For the compose stack the database was restored from a `pg_dump` of the dev database (`pg_restore --clean`). `production.md` does not say how a fresh production database is initialised (the schema migration image is mentioned in build-process only as a flag). `compose-postgresql-https` is not usable as shipped here (Traefik + traefik.me certificate, external volumes, the app has no filestore volume: the doc's own known issue). "}
{"id": "WR19-4", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**Keycloak admin password for the realm synchronizer is `judo`**: with another `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD` the application cannot create the realm (stack trace `KeycloakConnector.getAdminClient`) and nothing in `application-config.md` tells which variable carries it. Compose uses `judo`. "}
{"id": "WR19-5", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**PostgreSQL `max_connections`**: the application with the default 100 connections gives \"sorry, too many clients\" after two restarts of the app container; compose sets 300. Not in `production.md`. "}
{"id": "WR19-6", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**No foreign-key indexes + derived members = slow checkout (found through the smoke failures of round 18).** `CustomerAccount` derived members (cart sums, loyalty, company flags) are one big SELECT whose joins over `t_webshop_cart_line`, `t_webshop_sales_order`, `t_webshop_points_entry` ... have no index; with 1 859 customer accounts a checkout took 20 s (the spec waits 20 s) and F71 / F76 failed. `scripts/dev-indexes.sql` (hand-made indexes) fixed it (F76 passed in 1.7 min). Slow queries were found with `log_min_duration_statement=500`. The model has no way to declare indexes (R18-2); the platform could index every foreign key by default. "}
{"id": "WR19-7", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**Interceptor operation names**: the built-in update of the admin product is `_updateInstanceWebshop_ProductInfo` and the seller's ends with `SellerProductInfo` (found in the existing interceptors, not in the doc: \"Operation FQN Format Reference\" explains the ASM form only). "}
{"id": "WR19-8", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**JIT account on the first call in the compose stack answers 403** (`~principal` of a brand-new Keycloak user): the interceptor creates the row but the first request fails (AUTHENTICATED_ENTITY_NOT_FOUND), the second works. Same in the dev stack, known since R7; the browser login repeats the call, an API client must call twice. "}
{"id": "WR19-9", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**F87 multi-shop tenancy: NOT built.** Read `multi-tenant-keycloak-realm.md`: a realm per shop needs a RealmManager over the Keycloak admin client and one client per realm for the actor (`azp`), plus the portal URL / OIDC authority per shop in the frontend; the other option (one realm, tenant column on Product / CustomerAccount / ShopConfig, tenant-scoped access expressions, tenant of the account from the client or the e-mail domain, hand-written backfill of the existing rows into a first shop) touches the catalogue, cart, orders, search SQL and the settings. Neither fitted the time that was left after F86, F88-F90 and the red smoke tests of round 18; nothing of it is in the model. The \"cannot log in to the other shop\" check needs separate clients / realms in any design. "}
{"id": "WR19-10", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**F88: real Web Push not built** (stub provider with polling): VAPID keys, a service worker and the browser push service are not reachable from a headless test; the catalog entry `push-notification-system` was found by search but not read to the end for lack of time. The stub is switched by the shop setting (succeed / fail / timeout) like carrier and mail. "}
{"id": "WR19-11", "src": "webshop-R19", "target": "", "text": "**F86 PDF**: the DOCX / XDocReport pipeline is marked legacy in the catalog; the PDF comes from the small Markdown renderer of F39. PDFBox is a `provided` dependency, so the integration tests cannot render it (checked in the browser spec with `pdftotext`: the text holds the days, the revenues and the total). ### Round 19: not done / open (written at the deadline) - **F87 not built** (R19-9). - **F88**: no real browser push (stub, polling every 4 s); only sub-order shipments push (an order without sub-orders shipped by the admin does not). - **F89**: the old `address` column is kept (read-only in the profile); the country part of old addresses is not kept (no country field); rows that do not fit the \"street, postal city\" shape keep everything in `street`. - **F90**: the stack starts from the Karaf distribution of this build in an `eclipse-temurin` container (no application image: `build -d` could not be run with the flags available, see below); the database was restored from a dump; `deploy/verify-restart.sh` shows orders, accounts, products, stored files and Keycloak users identical after `docker compose down && up` (run once: SAME). The restart proof is not part of the Playwright spec (it stops containers). `build -d -M -B -F -KA` prints \"Building version SNAPSHOT\" and builds nothing (no goal is left), and `build -d` alone stops and deletes the running Karaf first (and aborts on \"Karaf is not running\"). - **Hand-made indexes** (R19-6) are not in the model. ### Round 19: smoke result and flaky list - `--grep @smoke` (serial, whole customer project, 21 tests): 19 passed, 2 failed. Both failures came from MY seed data and are fixed: (1) `level10b F86` expected the totals of its own orders but an earlier run had seeded orders on the same days (fixed: a year of its own per run); (2) `level9a F72` could not open its order in the back office because the future-dated orders of F86 / F88 (year 2097 and later) sat on top of the \"newest first\" list (fixed: `scripts/clean-future-orders.sql`, run by the spec after each test). After the fixes: `level9a F72` passes alone (34 s), `level10b` passes 3/3 (46 s). The full smoke run was NOT repeated (time): the final state of the 21 smoke tests is therefore \"19 passed in the run, the 2 fixed ones passed alone\". - Seeded future-dated orders are a trap for every spec that sorts newest first: seed with a date of the present and your own marker instead (to do). "}
